From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:55:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(glm cuda): DFlash2 for several streams: batched block
 passes and context updates (each stream's solo bits)

dflash2_multi.MultiDrafter drafts up to 4 streams from one Drafter's weights, each from its own context ring
(DraftContext, which stands in for a solo drafter in prefill, snapshots and restores):

- block passes of several streams in one launch sequence: every kernel of a pass is row-independent except the
  block attention, which reads each stream's own ring (a segmented kernel), and the selector projection and top-k,
  which run per stream on its rows alone
- context updates stack every stream's kept rows, each row with its own position and ring destination
- CUDA graphs for 1..streams block passes and for update row buckets (padding rows go to trash rows)

dflash2.py: merge_candidates (the solo candidates' merge, shared), a SEG flag on the dynamic convolution (blocks side
by side), and Drafter.chain(confs=...) to walk a chain whole and report each pick's confidence (the picks unchanged).

Tests (GPU): tests/cuda/test_glm_draft_multi.py: 1-4 streams at different lengths (ring wrapped, flat buffers),
eager and graphs, two ranks as threads, against one solo Drafter per stream, bit for bit; 4-bit matmul rows
independent of the row count at the real drafter's shapes.

From the GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Sparks recipe (MiaAI-Lab), patch 0027.

